When testing components that communicate via props and events, you can:
- Set props and assert the rendered output.
- Trigger events (e.g., `wrapper.find('button').trigger('click')`) and check that the correct event was emitted.

```javascript
test('emits add event on button click', () => {
  const wrapper = mount(ProductCard, { props: { product } });
  wrapper.find('button').trigger('click');
  expect(wrapper.emitted('add')).toBeTruthy();
});
```
